  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda - Larvae production facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a start-up financing from DGGF, Marula Agribusiness B.V. (&apos;Marula&apos;) will be able to further  develop the existing larval production facility together with the local subsidiary:a nursery and processing facility (based on circular waste) for Black Soldier larvae (maggots), which will be used as protein and fat component in animal feed for poultry /tilapia in particular. The residual waste will be used as fertilizer for agriculture in Uganda.The pilot of the local company started at the beginning of 2018 with the help of a DGGF TA subsidy and has been successfully concluded. Marula therefore wants to expand the current production capacity.The impact of this project is huge. For example, this project offers a solution to the major waste problem in the country and also ensures a reliable and affordable component for animal feed (poultry sector / tilapia production) and thereby contributes to reliable food consumption. The production and processing facility also provides additional employment (growth of 50 people). After a successful roll-out of the pilot in the first location, the team wants to expand to six locations in total.</narrative>
  </description>
